*======================================================================
* shared.a99 - what the two modules agree on: their colours and the
* variables they share in slot A.  Included by both.  (Modules share
* state only through slot A addresses fixed like this.)
*======================================================================
* Colour attributes for both modules, written out once so that they agree (see
* examples/hello for what an attribute is).
ANORM  EQU  (RTEXT*16+RBG)*256
ABAR   EQU  (RBARFG*16+RBARBG)*256
ASEL   EQU  (RSELFG*16+RSELBG)*256
AMARK  EQU  (RMARK*16+RBG)*256
AERR   EQU  (RERROR*16+RBG)*256

* Modules cannot see each other's labels, only the numbers both have been
* given, so shared state is declared once in a file both COPY, at fixed
* addresses in APPRAM.  APPRAM is not cleared or moved when the kernel
* switches modules, so these keep their values across a trip through the
* viewer.  The browser's variables are first, the viewer's follow them.
* the browser's variables (APPRAM, so they survive a trip through the viewer)
NFILES EQU  APPRAM+0           files found in the catalog (at most MAXF)
SEL    EQU  APPRAM+2           the selected one
DISKSZ EQU  APPRAM+4           the disk's sectors
DISKFR EQU  APPRAM+6           ... free
MSGNO  EQU  APPRAM+8           the message to show (0: none)
EPTR   EQU  APPRAM+10          work: the entry being filled
DNAME  EQU  APPRAM+16          the disk's name, length-prefixed (11 bytes)
ENTS   EQU  APPRAM+32          the files: MAXF entries of 16 bytes
*                              +0 name (length-prefixed, 10 characters at most)
* +12 type (1 DIS/FIX 2 DIS/VAR 3 INT/FIX 4 INT/VAR 5 program)
*                              +14 size in sectors
MAXF   EQU  20
RECBUF EQU  ENTS+(MAXF*16)     a catalog record (38 bytes)
EEND   EQU  RECBUF+40
* the viewer's variables, above the browser's
* the file name: DSK1.NAME, length-prefixed (20 bytes)
VNAME  EQU   EEND
NLINES EQU  VNAME+20           lines loaded
TOPLN  EQU  VNAME+22           the line at the top of the screen
VPAGES EQU  VNAME+24           8 words: the SAMS page of each 51 lines
LINBUF EQU  VNAME+40           a line as read (80 bytes)
VWORK  EQU  VNAME+130          scratch words
LPP    EQU  51                 lines per page: 51 * 80 = 4,080 bytes
